{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And I will bless your bread and your water.</b> Let blessing be found in them. All kinds of food are called 'bread' and all kinds of drink are called 'water,' as it is written, ״לחמי ומימי״ (my bread and my water). And Scripture answers accordingly: ״והשבתי לכם את הדגן וגו׳״ — therefore, ״אשיב לכם וגו׳, והשבתי את דגני בעתו ותירושי במועדו״. It should have said 'my water.'" "<b>And I will remove illness from your midst.</b> So that you be healthy — for what good is food to a sick person who cannot eat?"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:08.892762249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}